ship. Adaptability? not open to new ideas? Not mentioned. Overall mixed.\n\n- B: Reliability: very conscientious. Stress: handles stress well. Technical: weather assessment, computer skills. Decision quality? not mentioned. Attention: weak memory for numbers. Communication: pretentious, wrong tone, nasty remarks. Crew cooperation: poor. Responsibility? not mentioned. Overall strong on some, weak on communication and attention.\n\n- C: Reliability: 100% reliable. Decision quality: can make correct decisions quickly. Crew atmosphere: positive. Communication: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric. Education: not willing to further education. Concern for others: puts concern for others above everything (positive). Technical competence? not mentioned. Stress resilience? not mentioned. Overall strong reliability and decision, but communication issues.\n\n- D: Responsibility: takes responsibility seriously. Problem solving: solves problems extremely well. Concentration: can concentrate very well. Handles unexpected events adequately. Concerns: hot temper, know-it-all, loner, arrogance, weak leadership. Communication? not mentioned but likely issues. Stress resilience? handles unexpected events. Decision quality? solves problems. Attention: concentration. Crew cooperation: concerns.\n\nWe need to pick best overall. The biggest safety-critical concerns are crew cooperation and communication, as they affect cockpit resource management. B's nasty remarks are severe. D's hot temper also severe. C's difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric may affect crew but he creates positive atmosphere and is reliable. A's unfriendly demeanor also problematic.\n\nThus C might be the best overall despite communication difficulty, because he is reliable, makes correct decisions quickly, positive crew atmosphere, and puts concern for others above everything. The egocentric and communication difficulty could be mitigated. Also he is 100% reliable. So I might recommend Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: mention that B and D have serious crew cooperation concerns, while C's strengths in reliability and decision quality outweigh his communication issues. Provide evidence: \"can make correct decisions quickly\", \"100% reliable\", \"creates a positive atmosphere with his crew\". Also note concerns: \"difficulty communicating ideas\", \"egocentric\", \"not very willing to further his education\". Argue that these are less safety-critical than B's nasty remarks and D's hot temper.\n\nThus my vote: Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: state my recommendation, reference prior discussion, give evidence, explain why C is preferred.\n\nMETADATA_JSON: vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
